# No em dashes in text

Do not use em dashes (`—`, Unicode U+2014) in user-facing portfolio copy.

## Use instead

- **Date ranges:** `to` (e.g. `Aug 2024 to May 2026`, `2025 to Present`)
- **Clarification or result:** comma, colon, or a short rewrite
- **Greeting / title:** comma (e.g. `Hello, I'm` not `Hello — I'm`)

## Examples

```
// BAD
"ML systems — better entity extraction"
"Aug 2024 — May 2026"
"Hello — I'm Aaditey"

// GOOD
"ML systems: better entity extraction"
"Aug 2024 to May 2026"
"Hello, I'm Aaditey"
```

En dashes in proper names (e.g. `Bradley–Terry`) and middle dots in labels (e.g. `Modeling · ML`) are fine.
